      <data key="d1">"BRASIL refers to the Brazilian government or health ministry."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brasil is the source of the provided text, likely referring to the Brazilian government or healthcare system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brasil refers to Brazil, the country where the study and related events take place."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brasil refers to the country of Brazil, likely the source of the health recommendations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brazil is mentioned as a location."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brazil is mentioned as the country of origin for the data presented in the text, specifically referring to the year 2008."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brazil is referenced as the country where these health policies and initiatives are being implemented."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brazil is the country where the Ministry of Health operates."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Brazilian government, specifically its health department (presumably) as this document seems to be outlining healthcare guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"The text mentions 'Brasil' in the context of providing medical guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"BRASIL refers to the government of Brazil, as mentioned in context about dietary guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brasil is the country where dietary recommendations are made, as indicated by 'Guia Alimentar para a População Brasileira'."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brazil is a country referenced throughout the text for its diabetes statistics and healthcare system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brazil, as represented by its Ministry of Health."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Brazilian government, represented through various health publications and guidelines."</data>
