    <node id="&quot;OBESITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A chronic disease characterized by excessive body fat accumulation, potentially impacting health."&lt;SEP&gt;"A specific health concern addressed in the text, linked to dietary choices and physical activity levels."&lt;SEP&gt;"Obesity is a chronic disease that affects individuals and their quality of life. It involves past medical history, current health status, treatments, surgeries, and genetic predisposition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Obesity is a health condition addressed in the provided guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Obesity is a health condition discussed throughout the text as a significant public health concern."&lt;SEP&gt;"Obesity is a health condition mentioned as one that can be addressed through physical activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Obesity is a medical condition characterized by excessive body fat, generally with an IMC of 30 kg/m² or higher."&lt;SEP&gt;"Obesity is a significant health concern addressed in the text, particularly regarding its impact on older adults."&lt;SEP&gt;"Obesity is the central health issue discussed in the text, affecting individuals socially and physically."&lt;SEP&gt;"Obesity refers to a condition characterized by excessive body fat accumulation, leading to health risks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Obesity refers to an excessive accumulation of body fat, often associated with health risks."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Obesity journal published a systematic review about obesity in older adults."&lt;SEP&gt;"This is the name of the journal where several studies are referenced."&lt;SEP&gt;"Obesity is a condition characterized by excessive body fat accumulation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Obesity is a medical condition characterized by excessive body fat."&lt;SEP&gt;"Obesity is excess body weight and fat, contributing to diabetes risk and complications."</data>
