    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SBC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sociedade Brasileira de Cardiologia (SBC) is a medical organization that focuses on cardiology."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3efcb0f7cafd7155d35721d743353421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SBN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sociedade Brasileira de Nefrologia (SBN) is a medical organization specializing in nephrology."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3efcb0f7cafd7155d35721d743353421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIPERTENÇÃO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hypertension refers to high blood pressure, a condition where the force of blood against artery walls is consistently too high."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3efcb0f7cafd7155d35721d743353421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIPERTENSÃO DO AVENTAL BRANCO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"White coat hypertension refers to elevated blood pressure readings specifically in a clinical setting but not during home monitoring."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3efcb0f7cafd7155d35721d743353421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIPERTENSÃO MASCARADA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Masked hypertension refers to high blood pressure that is only apparent during ambulatory or home monitoring and not in a clinic setting."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3efcb0f7cafd7155d35721d743353421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MONITORIZAÇÃO AMBULATORIAL DA PA (MAPA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ambulatory blood pressure monitoring involves continuous recording of blood pressure readings over a 24-hour period."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3efcb0f7cafd7155d35721d743353421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AUTOMEDIDA DA PA (AMPA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Self-measured blood pressure refers to blood pressure readings taken by individuals themselves at home."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3efcb0f7cafd7155d35721d743353421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MONITORIZAÇÃO RESIDENCIAL DA PA (MRPA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Home blood pressure monitoring involves regular measurement of blood pressure in a person's own residence."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3efcb0f7cafd7155d35721d743353421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLIÚRIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Excessive urination."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyuria refers to excessive urination, often associated with diabetes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyuria refers to excessive urination, often associated with hyperglycemia and diabetes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-11829232da34e8f31cf6f7248c9b2229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8fbdcca6142a11665b95bb70d17aa20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3efcb0f7cafd7155d35721d743353421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLIDIPSIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Excessive thirst."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polydipsia refers to excessive thirst, also commonly linked to diabetes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polydipsia refers to excessive thirst, often associated with hyperglycemia."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-11829232da34e8f31cf6f7248c9b2229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8fbdcca6142a11665b95bb70d17aa20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3efcb0f7cafd7155d35721d743353421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLIFAGIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Excessive hunger."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyphagia is characterized by increased hunger and a desire to eat more than usual, frequently seen in diabetes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyphagia is the symptom of excessive hunger or increased food intake."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-11829232da34e8f31cf6f7248c9b2229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8fbdcca6142a11665b95bb70d17aa20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3efcb0f7cafd7155d35721d743353421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLICEMIA DE JEJUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Blood glucose level measured after a period of fasting."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fasting blood glucose refers to a blood sugar level measured after an overnight fast."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glicemia de jejum refers to a blood glucose test performed after fasting for at least 8 hours."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8fbdcca6142a11665b95bb70d17aa20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3efcb0f7cafd7155d35721d743353421&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b1ef5d792a0c1811c23cf9fb53f9976</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TESTE ORAL DE TOLERÂNCIA À GLICOSE (TTG-75 G)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MEASUREMENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oral glucose tolerance test measures the body's response to consuming a standardized amount of glucose."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3efcb0f7cafd7155d35721d743353421</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLICEMIA CASUAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Blood glucose level measured at any time of day, regardless of the last meal."&lt;SEP&gt;"Random blood glucose refers to a blood sugar level measured at any time without regard to meal timing."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f8fbdcca6142a11665b95bb70d17aa20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3efcb0f7cafd7155d35721d743353421</data>
