    <node id="&quot;DIABETES MELLITUS (DM)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A metabolic disorder characterized by high blood sugar levels and disturbances in carbohydrate, protein, and fat metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diabetes Mellitus (DM) is a chronic condition mentioned throughout the text and forms the basis of healthcare interventions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diabetes Mellitus (DM) refers to a group of metabolic disorders characterized by elevated blood glucose levels."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diabetes Mellitus, often abbreviated as DM, is a chronic metabolic disorder characterized by elevated blood sugar levels."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diabetes mellitus is a chronic metabolic disorder characterized by elevated blood sugar levels."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diabetes mellitus, often referred to as DM, is a chronic metabolic disorder characterized by high blood sugar levels."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2719c5ac33e4d4354d6e811f32b4f68c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94bcf07fd12315beb6d8cd3606b7aee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a09851ef900b6d5e9033f390f25ba516&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ec7e793644f66b20771251148afdb88&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c53ed59f6b0e98e93fb5837fe2400963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10ba5d9481de4afdef97e47b4183a521</data>
